  "user_request_original": "Design a 25-layer defect-cavity bandpass filter on fused silica substrate using Ta2O5 and SiO2. Stack sequence: Air | (Ta2O5|SiO2)_6 | Ta2O5(cavity) | (SiO2|Ta2O5)_6 | Fused Silica. Initialize all DBR layers with thicknesses scaled to 0.7× deviation from quarter-wave targets at 1550 nm (Ta2O5 nominal 126 nm, SiO2 nominal 189 nm). Fix central cavity layer (layer index 12, 13th layer) at exactly 540.0 nm. Allow all other 24 layers to be optimized via gradient-based thickness optimization. Evaluate coherent TMM transmittance at normal incidence for unpolarized light across 1400-1700 nm. Target high transmittance at 1550 nm with suppression in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm bands. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 1400-1500 nm, 1550-1550 nm, 1600-1700 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance at 1550 nm (soft target ≥ 0.95); strong suppression of transmittance in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 1400-1500 nm; transmittance in 1600-1700 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layers ≤ 30.",
